lesson: 180
title: Olympiad puzzle: how many pages from the digits?
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: Numbering pages from 1: pages 1 to 9 use 9 digits, pages 10 to 99 are 90 pages of 2 digits, 180 digits; together 189 digits.
explain: From page 100 on, every page uses 3 digits.
explain: A book used 552 digits: 552 - 189 = 363 digits are on three-digit pages, 363 / 3 = 121 such pages.
explain: They are pages 100, 101, …, so the last page is 99 + 121 = 220. The book has 220 pages.
vars: a=name p=100..400 k=3..12
let: D = 3 * p - 108
answer: p
exercise: The pages of a book are numbered 1, 2, 3, and so on. To print all the page numbers, {D} digits were used. How many pages does the book have?
exercise: {a} writes all the whole numbers from 1 up to some number, one after another. {a.He} writes {D} digits in all. What is the last number {a.he} writes?
exercise: The houses on a long street are numbered 1, 2, 3, … The metal digits for all the house numbers came to {D} digits. How many houses are on the street?
exercise: Numbering the pages of a diary from 1 needs {D} digits. How many pages does the diary have?
exercise: A printer numbers the tickets for a concert from 1 onwards and uses {D} digits in all. How many tickets are there?
test: Writing the numbers 1, 2, 3, … all the way to the number of the last seat in a stadium takes exactly {D} digits. How many seats does the stadium have?
test: A book has {k} colour pictures and a hard cover. Its pages are numbered from 1, and the page numbers use {D} digits altogether. How many pages are in the book?
test: {D} digits were typed when {a} numbered every page of {a.his} story, starting at 1. What is the number of the last page?
test: Lockers in a school are numbered from 1 to the last one. A sign-maker cut out {D} digits for these numbers. How many lockers are there?
exercise: How many pages does a book have if its page numbers, starting at 1, use {D} digits in all?
exercise: {a} in Ohio numbers the pages of a scrapbook 1, 2, 3, … and writes {D} digits in total. How many pages does the scrapbook have?
exercise: A theatre in London numbers its seats from 1 on. The seat numbers use {D} digits altogether. How many seats are there?
exercise: Pages numbered from 1; {D} digits used. How many pages?
exercise: A teacher in Toronto writes the numbers 1, 2, 3, … on raffle tickets, one number per ticket, and uses {D} digits combined. How many tickets are there?
exercise: To number the stamps in an album from 1 upward, {a} wrote {D} digits. How many stamps are in the album?
exercise: Every parking space in a car park in Sydney is numbered, starting at 1. The painter painted {D} digits. How many parking spaces are there?
exercise: The days in a diary in Dublin are numbered from 1, and writing all the numbers took {D} digits. How many days are numbered?
test: How many boxes are in a warehouse in Texas if they are labelled 1, 2, 3, … up to the last box and the labels use {D} digits?
test: A comic book has {k} stories. Its pages are numbered from 1, and all the page numbers together contain {D} digits. How many pages does it have?
test: Starting with 1, a machine in a factory in Birmingham stamps a number on each bottle, and so far it has stamped {D} digits. How many bottles has it stamped?
test: {D} digits are needed to number all the runners in a marathon in Auckland from 1 upward. How many runners are there?
test: The rooms of a big hotel in Las Vegas are numbered 1, 2, 3, and so on to the last room. If {D} digits are painted on the doors, how many rooms are there?
test: {a} writes down every number from 1 up and stops at some number; by then {a.he} has written {D} digits. At which number did {a.he} stop?
exercise: book pages numbered 1 2 3 n so on, printing all the numbers took {D} digits. how many pages
exercise: {a} wrote 1, 2, 3... all the way up, {D} digits total. what's the last number
exercise: page numbers used {D+3} digits — no wait, {D} digits. how many pages in the book
exercise: {a}'s numbering pages of a scrapbook from 1, used {D} digits, took {a.him} {k} hours lol. how many pages
test: book's pages numbered from 1, {D} digits used. Sam says that's {D} pages. nah, how many pages really
test: numbering tickets from 1 up, ran through {D} digits. how many tickets
test: to stamp numbers 1, 2, 3, ... on the pages it took {D} digits, oh and the cover's got none. how many pages has it got
exercise: When Grandad passed away, he left a diary whose pages are numbered 1, 2, 3, and so on. Printing all the page numbers used {D} digits. How many pages does the diary have?
exercise: printer "had a funny turn" (died) right after doing all the page numbers, {D} digits. how many pages in the stupid book then
test: The publisher was economical with the truth and called the book "short". Yet numbering its pages from 1 took {D} digits. How many pages are there?
exam: The pages of a volume being numbered consecutively commencing with 1, it is given that the aggregate number of digits employed in the printing of all page numbers is {D}. Determine the number of pages of the volume.
exam: It is given that {a} inscribes every whole number from 1 to a certain number inclusive, in succession, employing {D} digits in total. Ascertain the final number so inscribed.
exam: Ascertain the number of tickets in a series numbered consecutively from 1, given that the printing of the numbers upon all tickets required a total of {D} digits.
exam: Whereas {D} digits in aggregate were required for the numbering of the pages of a ledger, the numbering commencing at 1 and proceeding without omission, state the number of pages of which the ledger consists.
